Just to set the record straight:

* Several distributions of the GNU utilities are available for use
under Windows. The most popular sets that include both diff and patch
are probably cygwin and mingw, but Microsoft also used to release a
set of POSIX utilities too, including diff (but not patch as I
recall).

* Even without any additional utilities, "fc.exe", distributed with
Windows since NT4, does much the same work as diff; although it cannot
output in a clean patch-compatible format, it can find the differences
for you.  And "findstr.exe" is a fairly capable replacement for grep,
in a pinch.



